  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tBookkeeping\n\t\tBookkeeping FAQs\n\n### How can we record Daily Shop Sales (Cards and Cash Sales)\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 18 Nov, 2021 at  2:34 PM\n\n\t\tNavigation: Bookkeeping > Select Client > Tasks > Journals\n\nWatch how to record daily shop sales here\n\nThere are two quick ways to do this:\n\n1. You may add the Cash Sales as a Journal from Bookkeeping>>Tasks>>Journals. In a Journal you would Debit the Account for \"Cash in Hand\" and Credit the \"Sales\" Account.\n\n2. Alternatively, you may record under Sales for Bank receipts. Navigate through. Bookkeeping>>Sales>>Receipts then click on \"+Receipt\".\n\nPlease refer below screenshots for more help.\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
  "bodyHtml": "\n\t<div class=\"breadcrumb\">\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions\"> Solution home </a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/9000115344\">Bookkeeping</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/folders/9000188520\">Bookkeeping FAQs</a>\n\t</div>\n\t<b class=\"page-stamp page-stamp-article\">\n\t\t<b class=\"icon-page-article\"></b>\n\t</b>\n\n\t<h2 class=\"heading\">How can we record Daily Shop Sales (Cards and Cash Sales)\n\t \t<a href=\"#\"\n            class=\"solution-print--icon print--remove\"\n \t\t\ttitle=\"Print this Article\"\n \t\t\tarial-role=\"link\"\n \t\t\tarial-label=\"Print this Article\"\n\t\t\tid=\"print-article\"\n \t\t>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"icon-print\"></span>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"text-print\">Print</span>\n \t\t</a>\n\t</h2>\n\t\n\t<p>Modified on: Thu, 18 Nov, 2021 at  2:34 PM</p>\n\t<hr />\n\t\n\n\t<article class=\"article-body\" id=\"article-body\" rel=\"image-enlarge\">\n\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://www.useloom.com/share/81cf4474a51b430cac8ca7c43df8459a\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Navigation:&nbsp;</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Bookkeeping &gt; Select Client &gt; Tasks &gt;&nbsp;</span><span style=\"background-color: initial; font-size: 16px;\">Journals</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><a href=\"https://www.useloom.com/share/81cf4474a51b430cac8ca7c43df8459a\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Watch how to record daily shop sales here</strong></a></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">There are two quick ways to do this:</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">1. You may add the Cash Sales as a Journal from Bookkeeping&gt;&gt;Tasks&gt;&gt;Journals. In a Journal you would Debit the Account for \"Cash in Hand\" and Credit the \"Sales\" Account.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">2. Alternatively, you may record under Sales for Bank receipts. Navigate through. Bookkeeping&gt;&gt;Sales&gt;&gt;Receipts then click on \"+Receipt\".</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"><br></span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Please refer below screenshots for more help.</span></p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9073987608/original/--uGMMnM3lTCchfV6qQBX4LJj9rNCZ_7gg.png?1553252602\" width=\"602\" class=\"fr-fic fr-dii\" data-filelink=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9073987608/original/--uGMMnM3lTCchfV6qQBX4LJj9rNCZ_7gg.png?1553252602\" data-fileid=\"9073987608\" data-uniquekey=\"1553252587470\" style=\"width: 1103px;\"></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><img src=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9073987609/original/VbxrESCwyezY50Pogz7LWswQfk6-o8u1PQ.png?1553252602\" width=\"528\" class=\"fr-fic fr-dii\" data-filelink=\"https://s3.amazonaws.com/cdn.freshdesk.com/data/helpdesk/attachments/production/9073987609/original/VbxrESCwyezY50Pogz7LWswQfk6-o8u1PQ.png?1553252602\" data-fileid=\"9073987609\" data-uniquekey=\"1553252587470\" style=\"width: 1103px;\"></p><p><br></p>\n\t</article>\n\n\t<hr />\t\n\t\t\n\n\t\t<p class=\"article-vote\" id=\"voting-container\" \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdata-user-id=\"\" \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdata-article-id=\"9000165343\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdata-language=\"en\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?<span data-href=\"/support/solutions/articles/9000165343/thumbs_up\" class=\"vote-up a-link\" id=\"article_thumbs_up\" \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdata-remote=\"true\" data-method=\"put\" data-update=\"#voting-container\" \n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdata-user-id=\"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdata-article-id=\"9000165343\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\